A||||33||skitime||Removeable Rear Window  ||||1||
Z||000000||skitime||08-21-2001||01:14 PM||||I keep getting questions and emails about this removable rear window in other threads. I hate to be taking threads in a direction that was not originally asked so I decided to make it its own tread.  <P>Question 1 - How did you do it?<P>Basically I removed the rear window. (Easier said than done see pics) I used the glass for a pattern to cut three pieces of glass. I made a channel to receive the glass at the bottom and holes in the center piece of glass to hold the hardware. Probably the hardest part was making a steel panel completely around the inside of the third brake light so it is strong and fastened to the steel of the roof. It appears that the latch mount is just screwed to the plastic but it screwed through the plastic and into the steel light frame. The hardware was found in a junkyard and is off a sunroof except the mount under the third brake light which I had Brucepts machine that part for me.<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7090002-1_1.JPG">     <P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7090009-1_1.JPG">     <P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7090004-1_1.JPG">    <BR> <BR>Question 2 - Do you get fumes?<P>Fumes are not a problem but you do get heat if the tops are off or windows are open.  On a cool evening it  is awesome because you are flooded with a warm breeze unlike a heater. It is kind of reverse of what you do normally. Usually you put a window down to cool the interior but now you can put a window down to warm the interior. With all the windows closed and the rear open it is great and function like the popped sunroof. One of the coolest features I like is the sound of the V6 is purring right in your ear.  It also allows a new position to work on the engine. If you remove the trunk you can actually see to work on the front manifold by sticking you head through the window. With the trunk window I was able to see the manifolds glow at night with someone else driving.<P> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7240001.jpg">        <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7240006.jpg">        <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7240004.jpg">       <P>Question 3. How did you come up with the idea?<P>Veronica has a white 88 GT with a sunroof. I like how you can pop the sunroof open while you are driving. I missed this feature in my t-top and started figuring how I could do something like it.  I originally wanted it to lower the window down but after working on a design decided you could not avoid interference with the engine and trunk hinges. <P>Where do you store it? <P>I made custom mounts under the hood at the same location sunroof Fieros store there sunroofs. <P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P8210001.jpg">     <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 08-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||sqoach||08-21-2001||01:32 PM||||That is awesome! Makes your Fiero that much more unique. Have I told you I love your car?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Very nice write-up too.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">   <P>84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)||||reg||14
Z||000002||skitime||08-21-2001||01:46 PM||||BTW, I did this to my car the day after I took the series of pics that everyone seems to like. Some thought I was a little crazy doing that to the car but my theory is "No guts no glory"  Thats a common saying on skiers clothing but I like it.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7080039-2_9.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7080045-1_4.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7080042-1_1.JPG"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||08-21-2001||02:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by isthiswhereiputausername?:<BR><B>That is beautiful Skitime!<P>How do you have it latched inside?<BR>And is it air/fume tight after its back in? <P>TIA   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Question - How do you have it latched inside?<P>Here is the latch closed from the inside.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P8210004_1.jpg"> <P>And here it the latch open.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P8210005.jpg"> <P>Question -  Is the window air/fume tight.<P>Yes, I can blast it with a hose without leaking ||||reg||1
