Z||000008||cadaver||08-21-2001||10:23 PM||||great job. But I do have to say one thing. Is that glass tempered? Or is it regular house glass. I emailed you with some other questions but you never replied.||||reg||1
Z||000009||skitime||08-21-2001||10:29 PM||||The side pieces are safety glass and the center piece is tempered glass like sunroofs. Safety glass is cheaper to make than tempered glass. I had one prototype center window cut from safety glass but it cracked from where the holes were drilled. That was a waste of money. Tempered glass can flex so it will not break. Safety glass cannot flex.<p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 08-22-2001).]||||reg||1
