Z||000019||coolcat||08-22-2001||05:39 AM||||Ski, The car looks great you and Aus should team up. I have just one question. How did you get your original real window out? I ask because I have been trying to take mine out of my wrecked GT for about 2 months now. I am so frustrated with it that I'm about ready to just bust it out and say "fine you wanna play rough, have it your way" SMASH   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> .But seriously the car is going to the melters soon and I would rather have the window out than let it go.<BR>Thanks for any advice you can give me.<P>Donovan<P><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headbang.gif">  Gettin good players is easy,gettin them to play together is the hard part<p>[This message has been edited by coolcat (edited 08-22-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000020||Haagster||08-22-2001||05:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by kempo:<BR><B>I'd love to do the same stuff you've done to yours, but then you can say that I'm a copy cat... hah... <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Isn't immitation supposed to be a form of flattery??? (With the exception of that immitation butter that they use at the movie theater) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_4.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000021||skitime||08-22-2001||07:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by coolcat:<BR><B>Ski, I have just one question.How did you get your original real window out? I ask because I have been trying to take mine out of my wrecked GT for about 2 months now. I am so frustrated with it that I'm about ready to just bust it out and say "fine you wanna play rough have it your way" SMASH   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> .But seriously the car is going to the melters soon and I would rather have the window out than let it go.<BR>Thanks for any advice you can give me.<P>Donovan<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Like I said at first (Easier said than done see pics). You have to cut the window out using wire. Talk to someone that works in a junkyard, they can give you tips.  I don't know why you want to take one out of a car that is going to be crushed. You can't use that glass anyway unless you put it in another Fiero. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||coolcat||08-22-2001||07:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by skitime:<BR><B>  I don't know why you want to take one out of a car that is going to be crushed. You can't use that glass anyway unless you put it in another Fiero. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I want it because its the only thing that I dont already have off, and heaven forbid that my new GT gets its back window broken, its always good to have a spare. Thanx for the wire idea I'll try that. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headbang.gif"> Gettin good players is easy,gettin them to play together is the hard part||||reg||1
Z||000023||gomobile||08-22-2001||10:23 AM||||Where did you find that awesome trunk lid? I ask cause I was going to do something different but I like what I see. Much nicer and it looks at lot better then a regular SCOOP. ||||reg||6
Z||000024||skitime||08-22-2001||11:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gomobile:<BR><B>Where did you find that awesome trunk lid? I ask cause I was going to do something different but I like what I see. Much nicer and it looks at lot better then a regular SCOOP. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, I made the trunk mods myself. I feel trunk scoops tend to ruin the lines and block what little vision the Fiero already has especially with the wing. I wanted to have additional cooling too. You would not believe the heat that comes through the trunk vent. That vent gets hotter than the side vents. I got my trunk ideas from the 2001 Ferarri Spyder 360.  That car has the window and vents over the mid engine too. I felt the Fiero engine was a sharp looking engine too and should be shown off all the time.  I try to make my mods so that to non-Fiero people they might think it was stock. If I can't do that way then I don't want to do it.<P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spider4-1.JPG">      <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spider6.jpg">     <P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7080043-1_1.JPG">      <P><p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 08-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000025||jimmybpei||08-22-2001||07:49 PM||||Hey Ski,<P>Looks like there arn't too many guys in here<BR>willing to do there own mods. too bad i didn't live down there. would be a good business ha ha. maybe some s-10s too.<P>dont mind if you put the pic of my yellow car on but will e mail you some of the car with tires on it. would reall like to see them myself.<P>would like to know what color your car is <BR>( the red one) <P>The caddy motor is going in the red car. just got it the other day. By looking at bubbas site it going to be abig job. oh well i'll send the heads of the the shop the get the big valves and work done in the mean time.<P>hoping to have both cars done before summer as well as finish my s-10 too.<P>talk soon <BR>jimmy B.||||reg||1
Z||000026||skitime||08-22-2001||08:07 PM||||Boy JimmyB, you bite off a lot to chew.  Wish you lived closer I would like to give a hand. That is one cool S10 you have. Even a rabbit couldn't hide under it.  Well, I know you are not afraid of mods.  You have done things I wouldn't even tackle.  <P>My car is the original red.  It amazing what new paint looks like compared to weather paint.  I have a 86 GT with the same paint number but you wouldn't ever guess.  Red get darker in time.<P>So now onto the caddy motor.  Email me lots of pics so I could do mine. I was thinking of maybe pulling the caddy cam and having it ground more aggresive.  Are you shaving the heads a little too?  ||||reg||1
Z||000027||jimmybpei||08-22-2001||08:21 PM||||Skitime,<P>havent yet looked into any performance stuff for the caddy motor yet but i will be porting out the manifolds and running bigger pipe with a free flow muffler. <P>If you have any suggestions would love to hear them, as well for the 2.8 upgrade. <P>like the extra lovered vent in your car, what did that come out of. e-mail me with that if you want to.<P>I'll have to get pic of my yellow car so i can use that as my signature.<P>Later <BR>Jimmy B.||||reg||1
Z||000028||BlackDragon||08-22-2001||08:24 PM||||would you ever do something like that for someone else? how much would you charge? i would try myself, but i doubt if i could do it, and make it work correctly. could you use the mounts off of a sunroof to make it? how does it clip into the bottom?||||reg||1
Z||000029||skitime||08-22-2001||11:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackDragon:<BR><B>would you ever do something like that for someone else? how much would you charge? i would try myself, but i doubt if i could do it, and make it work correctly. could you use the mounts off of a sunroof to make it? how does it clip into the bottom?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I am considering making sometype of kit but I alway get onto another project which occupies my time.<P>The Fiero sunroof latch does not lend itself to being used as the latch mechanism. <P>I made a channel to recieve and seal the bottom of the glass. I had to design it so water could not enter into the interior by making the channel lower on the outside.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000030||gomobile||08-24-2001||11:13 PM||||I wrote to you before and all I can say is that I am going to try a similar project. My only question would be would you mind giving me your window measurments and most of all where did you get the long vent for the trunk.<P>Thanks<P>PS: I bet if you wrote the schematics and such you could make some extra $$$$.<P>And lastly was it hard popping out the back window?????<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by skitime:<BR><B>I keep getting questions and emails about this removable rear window in other threads. I hate to be taking threads in a direction that was not originally asked so I decided to make it its own tread.  <P>Question 1 - How did you do it?<P>Basically I removed the rear window. (Easier said than done see pics) I used the glass for a pattern to cut three pieces of glass. I made a channel to receive the glass at the bottom and holes in the center piece of glass to hold the hardware. Probably the hardest part was making a steel panel completely around the inside of the third brake light so it is strong and fastened to the steel of the roof. It appears that the latch mount is just screwed to the plastic but it screwed through the plastic and into the steel light frame. The hardware was found in a junkyard and is off a sunroof except the mount under the third brake light which I had Brucepts machine that part for me.<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7090002-1_1.JPG">      <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7090009-1_1.JPG">      <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7090004-1_1.JPG">     <BR> <BR>Question 2 - Do you get fumes?<P>Fumes are not a problem but you do get heat if the tops are off or windows are open.  On a cool evening it  is awesome because you are flooded with a warm breeze unlike a heater. It is kind of reverse of what you do normally. Usually you put a window down to cool the interior but now you can put a window down to warm the interior. With all the windows closed and the rear open it is great and function like the popped sunroof. One of the coolest features I like is the sound of the V6 is purring right in your ear.  It also allows a new position to work on the engine. If you remove the trunk you can actually see to work on the front manifold by sticking you head through the window. With the trunk window I was able to see the manifolds glow at night with someone else driving.<P> <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7240001.jpg">         <BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7240006.jpg">         <BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7240004.jpg">        <P>Question 3. How did you come up with the idea?<P>Veronica has a white 88 GT with a sunroof. I like how you can pop the sunroof open while you are driving. I missed this feature in my t-top and started figuring how I could do something like it.  I originally wanted it to lower the window down but after working on a design decided you could not avoid interference with the engine and trunk hinges. <P>Where do you store it? <P>I made custom mounts under the hood at the same location sunroof Fieros store there sunroofs. <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P8210001.jpg">      <P><BR>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 08-21-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||6
Z||000031||skitime||08-24-2001||11:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gomobile:<BR><B>I wrote to you before and all I can say is that I am going to try a similar project. My only question would be would you mind giving me your window measurments and most of all where did you get the long vent for the trunk.<P>Thanks<P>PS: I bet if you wrote the schematics and such you could make some extra $$$$.<P>And lastly was it hard popping out the back window?????<P> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What is the measurement of the center window?<P>I made it the width if the trunk.<P>Where did you get the long vent for the trunk?<P>I made the vent myself.<P>I bet if you wrote the schematics and such you could make some extra $$$$.<P>No but I teach drafting so I could easily. I definitely could use extra money with one daughter in college and another one will be soon.  hehe<P>And lastly was it hard popping out the back window?????<P>Yes, It was hard the first time. I did one in a yard to practice. (Anyone need a rear window? I got two.) The second time it went much easier.  You need to cut it out using a wire after the headliner, firewall cover, trunk, B pillar panels, computer cover, engine grills, fasback window inside trim and seats are removed. Popping is probably not the correct description. It is a very labor intensive operation. (Lots of sweat) <P>||||reg||1
Z||000032||Fierokid87||08-25-2001||12:09 AM||||Ski, maybe you and I should meet so you can give me a hand with ideas for my notch back 87 Fiero.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLOODY"> Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fieroguy1987<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000033||skitime||08-25-2001||12:29 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierokid87:<BR><B>Ski, maybe you and I should meet so you can give me a hand with ideas for my notch back 87 Fiero.<P>Scott<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hey, Scott I would love to meet sometime.  I think there are a lot of awesome things that haven't been done to a notchback yet. And I love the 87-88 body style. It ripe for mods.<P>Dave<P><p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 08-25-2001).]||||reg||1
